0,"evidenceId":"ev-5a052ec6f1a54285e132"},{"path":"server/api/v1/memo_share_service.go","line":172,"evidenceId":"ev-1991256de6c32c2d24e5"}],"candidates":[],"totalMatches":9,"truncated":false}}]},{"kind":"delivery-repair","value":{"candidate":{"schemaVersion":"authorization-inquiry-result/v1","questions":[{"questionId":"q1","behavior":{"disposition":"conditional","explanation":"GetSharedMemo is exposed without authentication and treats the supplied string as a bearer share-token lookup. A token first has to resolve to an existing, unexpired MemoShare; its stored MemoID then selects the memo. The request succeeds only if subsequent memo-state, visibility, structural, read-context, and conversion checks pass. A successful response is the selected memo, with reactions and attachments, but with Parent explicitly removed; the token does not authorize the surrounding conversation or relation graph."},"branches":[{"id":"invalid-token","condition":"No MemoShare is found for the supplied token, including a token that is not present in the backing store.","disposition":"deny","explanation":"getActiveMemoShare queries by UID/token. Store lookup returns nil when there is no match, and GetSharedMemo returns NOT_FOUND. The SQLite driver applies the UID equality predicate and maps no rows to nil.","evidenceIds":["ev-c9c7febb265c3f1a83ca","ev-100dea42d05fba30c476","ev-57ae47702fe790f1d0ed"]},{"id":"expired-token","condition":"The matched share has a non-nil ExpiresTs and the current Unix time is greater than that value.","disposition":"deny","explanation":"Expiry is checked after lookup. An expired share is treated as absent and returns NOT_FOUND, the same externally visible result as an invalid token; a nil expiry is represented as non-expiring in MemoShare.","evidenceIds":["ev-c9c7febb265c3f1a83ca","ev-100dea42d05fba30c476"]},{"id":"valid-token-memo-binding","condition":"The token resolves to a non-expired MemoShare whose MemoID identifies an existing memo.","disposition":"conditional","explanation":"The service calls GetMemo using ID equal to ms.MemoID. Thus the token-to-resource binding is the stored MemoShare.MemoID association, not a caller-supplied memo identifier. The visible store contract describes MemoShare as a bearer grant and includes MemoID; the shown driver query retrieves the share by UID.","evidenceIds":["ev-c9c7febb265c3f1a83ca","ev-100dea42d05fba30c476"]},{"id":"memo-state-and-audience-gates","condition":"The bound memo is missing, not Normal, or has SpaceAudience visibility.","disposition":"deny","explanation":"GetSharedMemo directly returns NOT_FOUND when memo is nil, not Normal, or SpaceAudience. This means archived memos are rejected on this path even though the general access policy has a separate archived/author rule. SpaceAudience memos are rejected before the share-specific read decision.","evidenceIds":["ev-c9c7febb265c3f1a83ca","ev-779026fbe150efcebc1d"]},{"id":"share-specific-read-override","condition":"The memo passes the service's preliminary checks and the access context contains SharedMemoID equal to the memo ID, with visibility other than SpaceAudience.","disposition":"allow","explanation":"The service passes &ms.MemoID into buildMemoReadContext. That resolves the current viewer, and for an unauthenticated viewer also resolves the instance anonymous-access setting, before calling ResolveMemoReadContext. CheckMemoReadContext makes a share apply only when the shared ID exactly equals the memo ID and the memo is not SpaceAudience; when it applies, it returns allowed before the ordinary Public/Protected/Private audience branches. Therefore a valid token can let an unauthenticated caller read a structurally valid Normal Public, Protected, or Private memo, subject to this endpoint's preliminary checks.","evidenceIds":["ev-c9c7febb265c3f1a83ca","ev-2de7448e6c715d4254da","ev-779026fbe150efcebc1d"]},{"id":"structural-and-creator-controls","condition":"The memo has an unknown visibility, invalid structural state, invalid/missing creator, or read-context construction/check fails.","disposition":"deny","explanation":"The access policy fails closed for nil/invalid creator, unknown visibility, invalid Space placement, and disallowed lifecycle state. GetSharedMemo maps a failed read-context check to NOT_FOUND. Separately, conversion requires the memo creator to be found; errMemoCreatorNotFound is also mapped to NOT_FOUND.","evidenceIds":["ev-c9c7febb265c3f1a83ca","ev-779026fbe150efcebc1d"]},{"id":"successful-payload-boundary","condition":"All preceding checks pass and reactions, attachments, and memo conversion succeed.","disposition":"allow","explanation":"The endpoint lists reactions and attachments for the bound memo and converts the memo. Conversion includes memo fields, reactions, attachments, and ordinary metadata. The endpoint passes nil relations to conversion, which yields an empty relation list, and then explicitly sets memoMessage.Parent = nil. The source comment states the token grants access to this memo only, not surrounding conversation or relation graph.","evidenceIds":["ev-c9c7febb265c3f1a83ca","ev-7c52afb43dac49bfe221"]},{"id":"ordinary-unauthenticated-access-without-token","condition":"An unauthenticated caller attempts ordinary memo access rather than this share-token path.","disposition":"conditional","explanation":"The share token is the exceptional authorization input on this path. Without a matching shared ID, the general policy requires the instance's AllowsAnonymousAccess setting for Public memos; Protected and Private memos deny an unauthenticated viewer, and SpaceAudience requires an authenticated member. This contrasts with a valid applicable share, which returns an allowed private-class decision for the exact non-Space memo.","evidenceIds":["ev-2de7448e6c715d4254da","ev-779026fbe150efcebc1d"]},{"id":"token-scope-boundary","condition":"The caller uses the same valid token to infer or fetch a parent memo, relation endpoint, or surrounding conversation.","disposition":"deny","explanation":"The source describes the share as memo-local and says relations never contribute access to either endpoint. GetSharedMemo removes Parent, supplies no relations, and the converter documents that Parent identity grants no access to the parent. The token therefore authorizes the returned memo's read, not adjacent resources.","evidenceIds":["ev-f78c832ca4a9f4e8f65c","ev-bf0c2319edbf8c6ab3c5","ev-779026fbe150efcebc1d","ev-7c52afb43dac49bfe221"]}],"evidenceIds":["ev-c9c7febb265c3f1a83ca","ev-100dea42d05fba30c476","ev-57ae47702fe790f1d0ed","ev-779026fbe150efcebc1d","ev-2de7448e6c715d4254da","ev-7c52afb43dac49bfe221","ev-499014a3fbd66b3b3a32","ev-574fec909f3dad8421d2","ev-a248ca5671b4d7d8e478"],"missing":[],"policyAssessment":{"status":"undetermined","explanation":"No normative authorization policy was supplied. The result describes observed source behavior and its limits only."}}],"observations":[],"scope":"usememos/memos@cb42e326ba9cc266a6a9570c53e0fe04c62793f4; allowed paths server/api/v1, core/access, store, proto/api/v1, internal/ratelimit. Investigated GetSharedMemo behavior only; no repository-wide coverage claimed."},"diagnostics":[{"code":"behavior-policy-assessment","path":"questions.0.policyAssessment","message":"Behavior has no normative policy comparison.","severity":"error"}],"instruction":"One diagnostics-only repair; preserve source judgments unless a diagnosed contradiction requires correction."}}]

